qa:AG18-QA-003
    a qa:Finding ;
    qa:findingId "AG18-QA-003" ;
    qa:phase "phase-AG" ;
    qa:title "Daemon dispatch still forks send-vs-ack before routing" ;
    qa:severity "blocking" ;
    qa:pattern "unresolved-dispatch-fork" ;
    qa:repeatable true ;
    qa:sourceReviewers "ruthless-boundary-qa (RBQA-F001)", "arch-qa (ARCH-004)", "req-qa (ATM-QA-003)", "AG.19 QA (ATM-QA-AG19-003)", "AG.20 QA (AG20-IMP-001)" ;
    qa:description """Original finding: dispatch_send in crates/atm-daemon/src/runtime_health/dispatch_delivery.rs:63-72 branched on `request.acknowledges_message_id.is_some()` into a separate ack path (ack_mail_with_runtime_and_post_send_emitter) before any single canonical routing decision, violating the AG.18 acceptance criterion (one canonical routing decision, not a send-vs-ack fork). AG.19's own QA (ATM-QA-AG19-003) and AG.20's own QA (AG20-IMP-001) each independently re-confirmed the identical fork, byte-for-byte unchanged, on their respective branches -- making this the single most-repeated cross-sprint finding in the AG ladder to date.

AG.21 (feature/pAG-s21-collapse-dispatch-routing, commit 56fdcdef, dev in progress -- this sprint's stated job is to delete this exact fork) was checked directly for this pass. dispatch_send in dispatch_delivery.rs (lines 56-102) no longer contains the acknowledges_message_id check; it now routes purely on route_send_request()'s Local/Remote (a legitimate, necessary host-routing decision, not the illegitimate send/ack fork), and calls a single function, execute_outbound_send_with_runtime_and_post_send_emitter, for all sends. However, that function itself (crates/atm-core/src/send/mod.rs:365-383) contains, verbatim:

    if request.acknowledges_message_id.is_some() && request.source_remote_host.is_none() {
        return ack_mail_with_runtime_and_post_send_emitter(...).map(SendResponseEnvelope::Acknowledged);
    }
    send_mail_with_runtime_and_post_send_emitter(request, ...).map(SendResponseEnvelope::Sent)

This is the identical fork, relocated one layer down from crates/atm-daemon into crates/atm-core, still executed before any canonical routing/send decision is made. AG.21 has moved the defect, not collapsed it -- the daemon-level symptom is gone but the underlying architectural violation (two divergent execution paths selected by a boolean flag check rather than a single canonical decision) persists and has simply migrated across the crate boundary into atm-core's send module.

Context note: the current integrate/phase-AG tip (commit 2cf19779, on an independent, more-advanced line not yet reachable from the AG.18-21 ladder) has resolved the equivalent decision structurally: RequestEnvelope::Send is itself typed as SendRequestEnvelope::Compose vs SendRequestEnvelope::Acknowledge, decided at parse/construction time rather than via a runtime boolean check inside a shared function, and dispatch() matches on that type directly. This is offered as an existing, in-repo exemplar of what a genuine architectural fix looks like, though it lives on a divergent line and does not itself close this finding for the AG.18-21 ladder.""" ;
    qa:sweepScope "repeatable-pattern sweep across AG.18-AG.21 worktrees for the acknowledges_message_id-based fork in dispatch_send (and its relocated successor)" .

