# --- Promotion determination ---

qa:AG18-QA-003-promotion
    a qa:PromotionDecision ;
    qa:finding qa:AG18-QA-003 ;
    qa:highestOpenBranch "feature/pAG-s21-collapse-dispatch-routing" ;
    qa:promoteToBranch "feature/pAG-s21-collapse-dispatch-routing" ;
    qa:rationale """All four worktrees with real commits (AG.18-AG.21) exhibit the same underlying defect: a boolean acknowledges_message_id check forks execution into a separate ack path before any single canonical send/route decision is made. AG.18 through AG.20 carry the fork verbatim and unchanged in crates/atm-daemon/src/runtime_health/dispatch_delivery.rs, independently re-confirmed by each sprint's own QA (ATM-QA-AG19-003, AG20-IMP-001) in addition to the original three reviewers (RBQA-F001, ARCH-004, ATM-QA-003). AG.21 -- the sprint explicitly tasked with collapsing this fork -- removed it from the daemon layer but relocated the identical check into crates/atm-core/src/send/mod.rs, one layer down; the architectural violation is unresolved, only moved. Per repeatable-pattern policy, the fix is dispatched once to the highest (latest) branch with real commits -- feature/pAG-s21-collapse-dispatch-routing -- since it is both the most-evolved state of the defect and the branch whose own mandate is to close it; AG.18-AG.20 close via merge-forward once AG.21 lands a genuine single-decision fix (e.g. deciding ack-vs-send once at request construction/parse time, mirroring the SendRequestEnvelope::Compose/Acknowledge type-level split already present on the independent, more-advanced integrate/phase-AG tip at commit 2cf19779 -- offered here as an in-repo exemplar, not as a mergeable fix for this ladder). AG.22-AG.25 are not yet started and are excluded from this sweep; re-sweep required once they carry real commits.""" .
